From 35f84d0c111ab85c2edf659e4ebcdd8c8267910d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 05:58:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Move the (now-unused) About hero video to Careers

The About page hero switched to a static image a while back, leaving
about-hero.mp4 sitting unused in the repo. Careers' hero video slot
had been wired up in the markup since earlier this session but never
actually had a file behind it (careers-hero.mp4 was never added), so
it's been silently falling back to a static poster this whole time.

Renamed about-hero.mp4 -> careers-hero.mp4 (and its poster frame to
match) and pointed careers.html's <video> at the new filename.

Note: I can't visually confirm autoplay in my own test browser here --
this sandbox's headless Chromium has no H.264 decoder at all
(canPlayType returns empty for H.264, "probably" for WebM only), so
every MP4 <video> fails to decode in my testing regardless of server
or markup. The file itself is a valid H.264/MP4 (verified with
ffprobe) and the wiring is identical to the pattern that worked for
About's video before, so it should autoplay fine in any real browser
-- just something to double check once this is live.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SjcntVjf5Nr2bdomgFdfPu
